        <h1 class="document-title">Markit EQT Trade Blotter</h1>
        <h2 class="document-subtitle" style="border:none; margin:0; padding:0; color:#475569; font-size:20px;">GWT vs ag-Grid Comparative Testing Framework: Architectural &amp; Technology Blueprint</h2>
        <div class="meta-info">
            <strong>Target Audience:</strong> Technical Leadership &amp; Stakeholders &nbsp;|&nbsp; 
            <strong>Prepared by:</strong> QA Automation Engineering Team &nbsp;|&nbsp; 
            <strong>Date:</strong> July 2026
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: Executive Summary -->
    <h2>1. Executive Summary &amp; Core Value Proposition</h2>
    <p>
        During major enterprise system migrations, such as transitioning the <strong>Markit EQT Trade Blotter</strong> from the legacy Google Web Toolkit (GWT) Old UI to the modern Angular/ag-Grid New UI, the most critical challenge is guaranteeing <strong>absolute parity</strong>. Every lookup criteria, trade detail record, date range filter, and visual component must render and compute exactly identical results across both versions.
    </p>
    <p>
        To solve this, we designed and implemented a <strong>100% Free and Open-Source Enterprise Testing Framework</strong> built on Node.js and Playwright. The framework automates parallel logins, runs dynamic searches against <strong>all 112 search criteria fields</strong>, scrapes complex grids, compares data row-by-row, and captures masked layouts. This ensures rapid regression detection without incurring expensive commercial software licensing costs.
    </p>

    <!-- Section 2: Architectural Flow Diagram -->
    <h2>2. System Architecture Flow Diagram</h2>
    <p>
        The framework operates on a modular, five-layered lifecycle: 
        <strong>1. Specification (BDD Brain)</strong> &rarr; 
        <strong>2. Orchestration (Playwright Engine)</strong> &rarr; 
        <strong>3. Browser Automation (POM Interfaces)</strong> &rarr; 
        <strong>4. Comparative Analytics (Parity Engine)</strong> &rarr; 
        <strong>5. Consolidated Reporting (Dashboard Output)</strong>.
    </p>

